          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Space Race</strong><br>\nKhrushchev's tenure is also marked by the Soviet Union's achievements in space, which began with the launch of Sputnik in 1957 and included sending the first human, Yuri Gagarin, into space in 1961.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ouster from Power</strong><br>\nKhrushchev's reforms, erratic behavior, and perceived political errors eventually led to his removal from power in 1964 by his party colleagues.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nDespite being ousted, Khrushchev is remembered for his significant contributions to the Soviet Union, including reducing the severity of Stalinist policies and propelling the nation into the Space Age.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
